                <pb facs="0616" n="577" xml:id="pg577"/>

                <head>278. Memorandum From Secretary of State Shultz to President Reagan<anchor n="1" xml:id="d278-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1988-05-17">May 17, 1988</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>[Omitted here is material unrelated to Morocco.]</p>
                <p>2. <hi rendition="#italic">Whitehead in
                        Morocco</hi>. John Whitehead met with
                    King Hassan May 12<anchor n="2" xml:id="d278-f2"/> to convey your letter to the
                        King<anchor n="3" xml:id="d278-f3"/> and to review regional issues. The King
                    criticized Shamir harshly saying his
                    policies were putting Israel in serious danger. He observed that a US peace initiative in an election year faced
                    severe challenges, but agreed we must continue the search for common ground.
                        Whitehead also met with Minister of
                    Interior Basri,<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d278-f4"/> who welcomed increased cooperation in combatting
                    narcotics production and trafficking. (S)</p>
                <p>[Omitted here is material unrelated to Morocco.]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
